{"id":"CVE-2014-0088","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-04-29T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T09:05:38.404Z","description":"The SPDY implementation in the ngx_http_spdy_module module in nginx 1.5.10 before 1.5.11, when running on a 32-bit platform, allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via a crafted request.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://mailman.nginx.org/pipermail/nginx-announce/2014/000132.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[nginx-announce] 20140304 nginx security advisory (CVE-2014-0088)"},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1030150","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1030150"}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-0133","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-03-28T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T09:05:38.993Z","description":"Heap-based buffer overflow in the SPDY implementation in nginx 1.3.15 before 1.4.7 and 1.5.x before 1.5.12 allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via a crafted request.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://mailman.nginx.org/pipermail/nginx-announce/2014/000135.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[nginx-announce] 20140318 nginx security advisory (CVE-2014-0133)"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2014-03/msg00095.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2014:0450"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/66537","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"66537"}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-3556","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-12-29T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T10:50:17.339Z","description":"The STARTTLS implementation in mail/ngx_mail_smtp_handler.c in the SMTP proxy in nginx 1.5.x and 1.6.x before 1.6.1 and 1.7.x before 1.7.4 does not properly restrict I/O buffering, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to insert commands into encrypted SMTP sessions by sending a cleartext command that is processed after TLS is in place, related to a \"plaintext command injection\" attack, a similar issue to CVE-2011-0411.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=142103967620673&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBOV03227"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1126891","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://mailman.nginx.org/pipermail/nginx-announce/2014/000144.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[nginx-announce] 20140805 nginx security advisory (CVE-2014-3556)"},{"url":"http://nginx.org/download/patch.2014.starttls.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-3616","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-12-08T11:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T10:50:17.280Z","description":"nginx 0.5.6 through 1.7.4, when using the same shared ssl_session_cache or ssl_session_ticket_key for multiple servers, can reuse a cached SSL session for an unrelated context, which allows remote attackers with certain privileges to conduct \"virtual host confusion\" attacks.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://mailman.nginx.org/pipermail/nginx-announce/2014/000147.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[nginx-announce] 20140916 nginx security advisory (CVE-2014-3616)"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2014/dsa-3029","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-3029"}],"vendors":["nginx"]}
